# Frontend conventions

Angular CLI workspace (not Nx): `customer-app`, `client-admin-app`,
`super-admin-app` plus shared libraries (`shared-ui`, `shared-data`, `auth`,
`layout`, `api-client`).

## Component style

- Standalone components (no `standalone: true` — implicit in v20),
  `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` everywhere.
- `input()`/`output()` functions, not decorators; `host` object, not
  `@HostBinding`/`@HostListener`.
- Native control flow (`@if`/`@for`), reactive forms only, `inject()` over
  constructor injection.
- Tailwind v4 first. CDK `Dialog` for overlays, CDK `BreakpointObserver` for
  responsive breakpoints.
- File naming has no `.component` suffix.

## Boundaries

- Path aliases (`@shared-ui`, `@shared-data`, `@auth`, `@layout`, `@api-client`)
  only across library boundaries — never deep relative imports into another
  project.
- Concrete per-domain stores extend `ListStore` at
  `src/app/shared/data/store/<domain>.store.ts` **inside each app**, not in
  `shared-data`.
- `api-client`'s `schema.ts` is generated — never hand-edit. Run
  `npm run openapi:generate`; `npm run openapi:check` is the drift check.
- Never hardcode API URLs. Use `src/environments/` wired via `angular.json`
  `fileReplacements`.

## Commands

`npm run start:{customer,client-admin,super-admin}` (ports 4200/4201/4202),
`npm run test:all`, `npx ng lint <project>` per project (no combined target),
`npx playwright test` (needs `docker compose up -d postgres redis backend` and a
migrate first — `globalSetup` seeds e2e users inside the backend container).
